index 9167187..a3ad090 100644
--- a/docs/partners.md
+++ b/docs/partners.md
@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 Acme Logistics receives `order.created` webhooks and validates every payload against
 `schemas/webhook_order_v1.json` (strict: unknown fields are rejected and the delivery is
 dropped). Any new field needs a v2 schema and 30 days' notice to Acme.
+
+`order_created_payload(order)` keeps the v1 payload unchanged and supports CNY
+orders only. EUR orders raise an error with v1 because its amounts implicitly
+mean CNY. Do not route EUR orders to a v1-only partner.
+
+The v2 schema is `schemas/webhook_order_v2.json`. It requires `currency` (`CNY`
+or `EUR`), with `amount_cents` in that currency's minor units. Use
+`order_created_payload(order, version=2)` only after the recipient has agreed
+to v2 and Acme's 30-day notice period has elapsed. This change does not switch
+existing partners to v2 or send that notice.
diff --git a/docs/runbook.md b/docs/runbook.md
index ac9990b..4597f33 100644
--- a/docs/runbook.md
+++ b/docs/runbook.md
@@ -5,3 +5,55 @@
 - Adding a column with a NOT NULL default rewrites the whole table on Postgres 10 and
   locks it for the duration (last time: 47 minutes of failed checkouts). Add the column
   nullable, backfill in batches of 10k, then add the constraint.
+
+## Currency rollout
+
+1. Apply `migrations/0007_orders_currency.sql`. Adding the nullable column and
+   then setting its default avoids a table rewrite. Old writers now default to
+   CNY; historical rows remain null until backfilled. During backfill, database
+   readers must interpret null currency as CNY (for example with
+   `COALESCE(currency, 'CNY')`). This repository has no database reader to update.
+2. Backfill in separate transactions of at most 10,000 rows. In psql, initialize
+   `\set last_id NULL`, run the statement below, then set `last_id` to the
+   returned maximum ID before each subsequent batch. Stop when `scanned_rows`
+   is zero. Commit each batch and throttle according to database load. The ID
+   checkpoint avoids repeatedly scanning all previously processed rows; existing
+   EUR values are preserved.
+
+   ```sql
+   WITH batch AS (
+       SELECT id FROM orders
+       WHERE (:last_id IS NULL OR id > :last_id)
+       ORDER BY id LIMIT 10000
+   ), updated AS (
+       UPDATE orders AS o SET currency = 'CNY'
+       FROM batch
+       WHERE o.id = batch.id AND o.currency IS NULL
+       RETURNING o.id
+   )
+   SELECT max(id) AS last_id, count(*) AS scanned_rows,
+          (SELECT count(*) FROM updated) AS updated_rows
+   FROM batch;
+   ```
+
+3. Deploy the currency-aware application. `CACHE_SCHEMA` is now 4, so new workers
+   ignore old cached Orders. Complete the worker rollout before accepting EUR:
+   old workers assume every amount is CNY. Ensure database writers/readers
+   persist and load the new field before enabling EUR intake.
+4. Once backfill and deployment are complete, enforce valid, non-null currencies:
+
+   ```sql
+   ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_currency_valid
+       CHECK (currency IS NOT NULL AND currency IN ('CNY', 'EUR')) NOT VALID;
+   ALTER TABLE orders VALIDATE CONSTRAINT orders_currency_valid;
+   ```
+
+   Run these as separate transactions. Validation scans the table while allowing
+   normal writes. Keep this validated check on PostgreSQL 10: `SET NOT NULL`
+   would scan the table under an exclusive lock even after check validation.
+5. Enable EUR only for partners ready for webhook v2, following
+   `docs/partners.md`. Finance dashboards must select each currency explicitly;
+   the existing default revenue total includes CNY orders only.
+
+This is a repository change; database rollout and partner notice are operational
+steps and have not been performed automatically.
